  "prompt": "I have 4 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) RESTOCK CART: From restock worklist `restock_worklist_wl2`, reorder each item flagged for reorder (skip reorder=false — the worklist also lists discontinued, renewed look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then add that many units to the cart. Then, from worklist `add_address_wl1`, save the new lakehouse shipping address: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `update_order_address_wl1`, redirect the pending order to the lakehouse address: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) STANDARDIZE ADDRESSES: From address worklist `address_worklist_wl2`, standardize each address entry needing standardization (skip needs_standardization=false — verified look-alikes are mixed in). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then update that address's country. Then, from worklist `cancel_order_wl1`, cancel the duplicated pre-shipment order: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `checkout_wl1`, place the standing supplies order at checkout: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) POST REVIEWS: From review worklist `review_worklist_wl2`, post each pending review (skip pending=false — already-reviewed look-alikes are listed). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then post the review on that product. Then, from worklist `ship_replacement_wl1`, ship the warranty replacement unit: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `remove_address_wl1`, delete the retired work shipping address: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) DISPATCH ORDERS: From fulfilment worklist `fulfil_worklist_wl2`, fulfil each paid order awaiting dispatch (skip the shipped/cancelled look-alikes — status must be paid). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then fulfil and dispatch it to that address. Then, from worklist `reship_order_wl1`, re-dispatch the returned-to-sender order: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `return_item_wl1`, start the return for the defective item: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 4 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
